{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":10688,"output":7331,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5286,"totalTokens":18019,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let me analyze each item.\n\nQ001: source \"Killed Shasshhiy'Kaish after letting her grow as powerful as possible.\" target \"在莎西·凯希成长到尽可能强大之后杀死她。\" \"killed her after letting her grow\" — target says \"杀死她\" after growing. Source implies \"after letting her grow as powerful as possible\" — the translation says \"成长到尽可能强大之后杀死她\". This is essentially same. \"after letting her grow\" vs \"在她成长到...之后\" — the nuance: player lets her grow, then kills. Target is fine. Actually target omits \"letting\" (让) — but semantically equivalent. No finding.\n\nQ002: source mentions Gorran, Cornac Archer; target \"科纳克人弓箭手，高岚\" — Gorran translated as 高岚. Names not verifiable. \"addlepated beardling\" → \"没脑子的毛脸小子\" — beardling refers to a young dwarf, but Gorran is a Cornac... anyway. Source: \"read the sign of the tavern in Last Hope from the tavern in Derth\" — target: \"坐在德斯镇的酒馆里就能看清最后的希望城酒馆的招牌\" — that's fine. \"I'm beginning to think that Sodelost has ulterior motives\" → \"苏达罗斯特另有所图\" — fine. Actually wait, source says \"Sodelost has ulterior motives\" but per context Sodelost is the dwarf rogue narrator of note 2... the speaker here is Gorran complaining about the dwarf (Sodelost, though he calls him a scout). Fine. \"lead us up this forsaken mountain to die just so he could rifle through our pockets\" → \"为了翻我们的口袋，故意把我们领上这座鬼山送死\" — fine. No obvious issue. \"beardling\" → \"毛脸小子\" — beardling means dwarf without beard (young), 毛脸 literally \"hairy face\" — reversed? beardling = a young/small dwarf; \"毛脸\" ok-ish. Not clearly objective defect.\n\nQ003: source \"I can give you a cloak that will conceal your true nature! With it all people will see when they look at you is a normal average Human. You can go about your business. Please!\" target \"我可以给你一件斗篷，它能隐藏你的真实本质！穿上它，任何人看到的都只会是一个普通人类，你便可以自由行事。求求你！\" Seems fine. \"normal average Human\" → \"普通人类\" fine. No finding.\n\nQ004: source \"Tales of the Spellblaze\" target \"魔法大爆炸的七章故事\" — \"seven chapters\" added! Source is just \"Tales of the Spellblaze\" with no chapter count. Context says eight chapters. So \"七章\" is an addition and contradicts context (eight chapters). FINDING: ADDITION, \"七章\", correction \"魔法大爆炸的故事\", evidence: desc \"Learned the eight chapters of the Spellblaze Chronicles.\"\n\nQ005: source \"Learned the eight chapters of the Spellblaze Chronicles.\" target \"阅读了有关魔法大爆炸的8章文献。\" — \"阅读\" vs \"Learned\" (习得/学会了). \"阅读了\" — learned vs read; reading is the means but \"learned\" is broader. Hmm. This is a slight shift but arguably ok. The bigger issue: \"Spellblaze Chronicles\" translated as \"有关魔法大爆炸的...文献\" — drops \"Chronicles\" title but acceptable. \"阅读了\" vs \"Learned\" — I'd consider minor. Not objective defect? Learned ≠ read strictly. I'd maybe flag UNCERTAIN. Actually the achievement is about knowing lore; 阅读了 is fine colloquially. I'll leave empty or UNCERTAIN. Given rule 4 UNCERTAIN only when evidence points to problem but real ambiguity. \"Learned\" → \"阅读了\" loses meaning of \"learned/mastered\". I'll call it... probably not a finding. Leave empty.\n\nQ006: \"Quest #CIMSON#Failed!\" target \"主线任务 #CIMSON#失败了！\" — \"Quest\" translated as \"主线任务\" (main quest). Source just says \"Quest\". This is a generic quest dialog used for all quests, including non-main quests. Adding \"主线\" changes scope. Context shows generic statuses. FINDING: SCOPE/ADDITION. \"主线任务\" correction \"任务\". Evidence: \"[Quest.FAILED] = _t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\"\" and context shows generic \"Quest #LIGHT_GREEN#Completed!\". FINDING.\n\nQ007: \"You must wear this object to use it!\" target \"你必须装备这件物品才能使用它！\" — wear → 装备, fine. No finding.\n\nQ008: source \"Click to copy to clipboard. You can share the wanderer seed with your friends, this way they can play with the same set of talents.\" target \"点击复制。你可以将流浪者随机种子分享给朋友，这样你们可以用同一套技能组合进行游玩。\" — \"wanderer seed\" → \"流浪者随机种子\" fine. \"Click to copy to clipboard\" → \"点击复制\" omits \"to clipboard\" but popup says copied to clipboard; minor omission. \"this way they can play\" → \"这样你们可以用\" — they → 你们 (you plural). Slight referent shift: source says friends can play; target says \"你们\" (you all) play with same talent set. Semantically similar. I think fine. No finding? \"Click to copy to clipboard\" → \"点击复制\" — omission of \"to clipboard\" is minor; I'd skip.\n\nQ009: \"Spare me the small talk. I am here to stop you!\" target \"我不是来和你们聊天的，我是来阻止你们的！\" — \"Spare me the small talk\" → \"我不是来聊天的\" — meaning shift: spare me the small talk = 别跟我客套/少废话. Target rephrases as \"I'm not here to chat\" — loses the imperative but conveys intent. Hmm, is this objective defect? \"Spare me the small talk\" is an imperative; target converts to statement. Meaning roughly preserved. Borderline. I'd say UNCERTAIN maybe. Actually the meaning is similar enough; I'll leave empty. Or report UNCERTAIN ACTION? I think it's acceptable localization. Skip.\n\nQ010: source \"Display mouse gesture trails\" target \"隐藏鼠标手势轨迹\" — Display → 隐藏 (hide). DIRECTION reversed! FINDING: ACTION/DIRECTION. Evidence from context: \"When you do a mouse gesture (right click + drag) a color coded trail is displayed.\" and status uses hide_gestures disabled/enabled. FINDING, claim_type DIRECTION, correction \"显示鼠标手势轨迹\".\n\nQ011: source \"This is the Way.\" target \"这不是维网。\" — negation added! \"This is the Way\" → \"这不是维网\" (This is NOT the Way). FINDING: DIRECTION/ADDITION. Also \"the Way\" translated as \"维网\" — weird term, but the negation is the clear defect. FINDING, target_span \"这不是维网\", correction \"这就是维网。\" Hmm, \"Way\" translation — \"维网\"? Possibly their established term. Correction: \"这就是‘道’。\" But I only have visible evidence for negation. Correction: \"这就是维网。\" Evidence: \"This is the Way.\"\n\nQ012: \"Open profile(in browser)\" target \"打开我的用户信息（在浏览器里打开）\" — \"profile\" → \"用户信息\" but context has \"Show infos\" → separate item; profile is 用户资料/个人主页. Also adds \"我的\". Hmm. \"Show infos\" is 用户信息 likely; profile is the online profile. Translating profile as 用户信息 conflicts with Show infos. But is that objective from visible evidence? Context shows both \"Show infos\" and \"Open profile(in browser)\". Translating profile as \"用户信息\" could collide. Borderline; \"profile\" → \"用户资料\" would be better. I'd report UNCERTAIN REFERENT/VALUE. Hmm, rule 3: added info compatible and not disprovable is not a defect. \"我的\" is fine. \"用户信息\" vs \"用户资料\" — subjective preference? The collision with \"Show infos\" is a real concern but we don't see its translation. I'll skip or UNCERTAIN. I'll skip—no strong objective defect.\n\nQ013: source \"which you do not understand: ...\" target \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解的文字：...\" — \"which you do not understand\" → \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解\" — addition \"即使你懂夏·图尔语\" — is it compatible? Context: this text appears when NOT speaks_shertul, i.e., player doesn't know Shertul. The addition claims \"even if you know Shertul language, you can't understand\" — actually in lore 4 (Q014 item's parallel) the text is undecipherable regardless. But can visible evidence disprove? The context shows player lacks speaks_shertul attr when this branch shows. Saying \"even if you understood Shertul, you couldn't understand\" is an addition but plausible (the language text remains untranslated even with the talent — in lore 2, with speaks_shertul you get translated text, so actually if you knew Shertul you WOULD understand: the else branch gives the translation \"But AMAKTHEL came...\". For lore 3, the else branch gives translation too. So the addition \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解\" contradicts the context structure: if player:attr(\"speaks_shertul\") then they get the translated version — meaning understanding Shertul WOULD allow comprehension. Hmm wait — for this lore (shertul-fortress-3), with speaks_shertul the translation is given. So the target's claim \"即使你懂也无法理解\" contradicts. But is the addition \"defect\" objective? The source says simply \"which you do not understand\". Target adds \"even if you know Shertul you cannot understand\" — that contradicts the code showing that knowing Shertul yields the translated text. FINDING: ADDITION (or VALUE). Evidence: \"(not game.player:attr(\\\"speaks_shertul\\\") and _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]] or _t[[#{italic}#'And AMAKTHEL made the SHER'TUL...\" — shows that when the player does understand Shertul, translated text is provided. I'll report FINDING ADDITION. Correction: \"你看不懂的文字：\" or \"你无法理解的文字：\".\n\nQ014: source \"Donated at least 16 euros to Tales of Maj'Eyal.\" target \"为马基·埃亚尔的传说捐赠至少 16 欧元，达到白银捐赠等级。\" — context: this is GOLD_DONATOR achievement (name = \"Gold Donator\", desc = SOURCE_MATCH_1). Target says \"达到白银捐赠等级\" (reached Silver donation tier) — contradicts context where Silver Donator is a separate achievement with 6 euros. FINDING: ADDITION/VALUE. target_span \"达到白银捐赠等级\", evidence: \"name = \\\"Silver Donator\\\", id = \\\"SILVER_DONATOR\\\"\" separate. Correction: remove \"，达到白银捐赠等级\" or say 黄金. Actually 16 euros = Gold tier. FINDING.\n\nQ015: \"Earned the rank of Destroyer in the arena.\" target \"在竞技场中获得“毁灭者”称号。\" — fine.\n\nQ016: \"DEBUG -- Alter Faction\" target \"调试模式 -- 锁定阵营\" — \"Alter\" → \"锁定\" (lock). ALTER ≠ lock. FINDING: ACTION. Evidence: the dialog lists factions and changes them (function _M:use... likely changes player faction). Context shows \"Alter Faction\" title. \"锁定阵营\" means lock faction. Correction: \"调试 -- 更改阵营\". FINDING.\n\nQ017: source \"which you do not understand: ...\" target \"你永远无法理解的文字：...\" — \"永远\" (never/forever) added. Source: \"which you do not understand\" — simple present. Target adds \"永远\" (can never understand). Addition. Is it disprovable? Context: if speaks_shertul, translated text given, so you could understand. But similar to Q013. Hmm, \"永远无法理解\" is a stronger claim not in source. Is this objective defect? The source says \"you do not understand\" — present state. Target says \"you will never be able to understand\" — different claim. I'd say FINDING ADDITION... or UNCERTAIN. Compare Q013 where the addition \"即使你懂夏·图尔语\" actively contradicts code. For Q017, \"永远\" is an addition without contradiction support... but code structure (translation provided when speaks_shertul) does undermine \"永远\". Both could be FINDING. But maybe be careful: the narrator might mean the strange runes are inherently incomprehensible. Actually for shertul-fortress-4, there's a translation branch, so with the talent you DO understand. So \"永远\" contradicts. I'll report FINDING ADDITION for both Q013 and Q017. For Q017 correction: \"你无法理解的文字：\".\n\nActually wait — for Q013, is the addition contradicted? The source_context shows shertul-fortress-3 with SOURCE_MATCH_1 being \"which you do not understand: ...\". The or-branch is the translation. So yes, understanding Shertul → translation. Contradiction supported. But hmm, subtle: \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解\" — could be flavor. Still, the evidence supports that knowing the language yields understanding. I'll mark FINDING for Q013 too. Alternatively UNCERTAIN for both to be safe? Rule 4: FINDING when evidence sufficient. The code structure directly shows understanding is possible via speaks_shertul. I'll go FINDING for both. Hmm, for Q013 the addition specifically contradicts; for Q017 \"永远\" also contradicts the availability of translation. Both FINDING, claim_type ADDITION.\n\nQ018: \"Got a character to level 50.\" target \"角色达到50级。\" fine.\n\nQ019: source \"Would it be possible for my Transmogrification Chest to automatically extract gems?\" target \"即使我不会提取宝石，也可以让我的转化之盒自动提取宝石吗？\" — addition \"即使我不会提取宝石\". Context: cond = \"player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS)\" — the question only appears if the player DOES know the Extract Gems talent! So the addition \"even if I don't know how to extract gems\" directly contradicts the condition. FINDING: ADDITION/CONDITION. Evidence: \"player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS)\". Correction: \"能让我的转化之盒自动提取宝石吗？\".\n\nQ020: \"The Legend of Garkul\" target \"加库尔的八章传说\" — \"八章\" (eight chapters) added; context desc says \"Learned the five chapters of the Legend of Garkul\" and lists garkul-history-1..5. FINDING: ADDITION. Correction \"加库尔的传说\".\n\nNow recheck Q005: \"Learned the eight chapters\" → \"阅读了有关魔法大爆炸的8章文献。\" Eight → 8 fine. \"Chronicles\" dropped but \"文献\" approximates. \"Learned\" → \"阅读了\" — hmm. Achievement desc pattern; other items? Not visible. I'll consider it acceptable. Leave candidates empty? Observation can note. Actually rule: no reportable objective problem → empty array. I'll leave empty.\n\nQ002: check more carefully. \"That addlepated beardling\" — beardling is a dwarf term; speaker Gorran insulting the dwarf Sodelost. \"毛脸小子\" — beardling = young beardless dwarf. \"毛脸\" (hairy face) is kind of opposite but insulting either way. Not objective. \"The finest eyes of the Iron Throne, able to read the sign of the tavern in Last Hope from the tavern in Derth!\" target: \"还说自己是钢铁王座眼力最好的家伙，坐在德斯镇的酒馆里就能看清最后的希望城酒馆的招牌！\" — \"from the tavern in Derth\" i.e., reading Last Hope's tavern sign from Derth's tavern. Target: \"坐在德斯镇的酒馆里就能看清最后的希望城酒馆的招牌\" — correct. OK empty.\n\nQ008: \"Click to copy to clipboard\" → \"点击复制\" — omits clipboard. Minor omission; \"点击复制\" implies copy. The popup later says \"Copied to clipboard!\". I'd leave empty. Also \"they can play\" → \"你们可以用\" — subject shift from \"they (friends)\" to \"你们 (you and friends)\". Target: \"这样你们可以用同一套技能组合进行游玩\" — \"你们\" includes the player; source \"they\" refers to friends. Minor. Not clearly a defect. Empty.\n\nQ009: I'll leave empty. Hmm, \"Spare me the small talk\" → \"我不是来和你们聊天的\" — Actually this changes a dismissive imperative into a declarative. The communicative function is similar (refusing small talk). I'll not report.\n\nQ006 double check: statuses map generic; \"Quest #CIMSON#Failed!\" — target \"主线任务\" — adding 主线. The dialog is for all quests (engine Quest dialog). Context evidence: statuses list generic quest statuses. FINDING SCOPE. correction \"任务 #CIMSON#失败了！\".\n\nQ012 reconsider: \"Open profile(in browser)\" → \"打开我的用户信息（在浏览器里打开）\". \"profile\" → \"用户信息\" — but \"Show infos\" also = 用户信息 likely, though its translation isn't visible. Not disprovable. \"我的\" addition harmless. Skip.\n\nNow Q004: is \"七章\" contradicted? Context desc: \"Learned the eight chapters of the Spellblaze Chronicles.\" and 8 knownLore checks. Yes FINDING. Target span \"魔法大爆炸的七章故事\". Correction \"魔法大爆炸的故事\". Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Learned the eight chapters of the Spellblaze Chronicles.]]\".\n\nQ010 evidence: \"When you do a mouse gesture (right click + drag) a color coded trail is displayed.\" and \"config.settings.hide_gestures\". Use \"a color coded trail is displayed\" to support 显示.\n\nQ016 evidence: \"Dialog.init(self, _t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", 1, 1)\" — hmm, that just shows title usage. Better evidence: the file context \"local Faction = require \\\"engine.Faction\\\"\" and GetQuantity — the dialog alters faction. The function name \"Alter Faction\". Evidence must appear verbatim in source_context. Use \"DEBUG -- Alter Faction\"? That's the source itself... evidence must be from source or source_context. I can use \"local Faction = require \\\"engine.Faction\\\"\" plus maybe \"self:use(item)\" — use(item) changes faction presumably. Let me just cite \"Alter Faction\" from source — evidence field must be verbatim from source or context. \"DEBUG -- Alter Faction\" is the source. Fine, evidence can be from source. Actually claim: Alter → 锁定 (lock) wrong; should be 更改/改变. Evidence: \"DEBUG -- Alter Faction\".\n\nQ011: also check \"I cannot, but I may show you a glimpse.\" → \"不行，不过我可以让你看一下。\" fine. \"He leans toward you. Your mind is suddenly filled with feelings of peace and happiness.\" → \"*他靠向你，你的脑海里突然充满了平静和幸福。*\" fine.\n\nQ011 correction: \"这就是维网。\" Hmm \"the Way\" — maybe better \"这就是‘维网’。\" Keep \"这就是维网。\" evidence \"This is the Way.\"\n\nQ013 correction: \"你看不懂的文字：\" — but keeping full span: correction could be \"你看不懂的文字：\". target_span: \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解的文字\". Evidence verbatim: \"(not game.player:attr(\\\"speaks_shertul\\\") and _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]] or _t[[#{italic}#'And AMAKTHEL made the SHER'TUL\" — need verbatim substring from context. Yes that string appears.\n\nQ017 evidence: \"or _t[[#{italic}#'We conquered the world\" — the translation branch. Or use \"not game.player:attr(\\\"speaks_shertul\\\")\". I'll use \"(not game.player:attr(\\\"speaks_shertul\\\") and _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]] or _t[[#{italic}#'We conquered the world\" — verbatim appears.\n\nQ019 evidence: \"and player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS) end}\" — verbatim: \"player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS)\". Target span: \"即使我不会提取宝石，也可以让我的转化之盒自动提取宝石吗？\" — must be verbatim in target: yes. Correction: \"可以让我的转化之盒自动提取宝石吗？\" claim_type ADDITION.\n\nQ014 target_span \"达到白银捐赠等级\". Evidence: \"name = \\\"Silver Donator\\\", id = \\\"SILVER_DONATOR\\\",\\n\\tdesc = _t[[Donated at least 6 euros to Tales of Maj'Eyal.]]\" — verbatim substring: \"name = \\\"Silver Donator\\\"\" appears. Correction: \"为马基·埃亚尔的传说捐赠至少 16 欧元。\" claim_type ADDITION.\n\nQ020 target_span \"八章\". Evidence: \"desc = _t[[Learned the five chapters of the Legend of Garkul.]]\" verbatim appears. Correction: \"加库尔的传说\". claim_type ADDITION.\n\nQ004 claim_type ADDITION.\n\nQ006 claim_type SCOPE. target_span \"主线任务\". Evidence: \"[Quest.FAILED] = _t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\"\" — verbatim appears? In context: \"[Quest.FAILED] = _t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\",\" yes. Correction \"任务 #CIMSON#失败了！\".\n\nQ010 claim_type DIRECTION. target_span \"隐藏鼠标手势轨迹\". Evidence: \"a color coded trail is displayed\". Correction \"显示鼠标手势轨迹\".\n\nQ011 claim_type DIRECTION (negation). target_span \"这不是维网\". Evidence \"This is the Way.\" Correction \"这就是维网。\"\n\nQ016 claim_type ACTION. target_span \"锁定阵营\". Correction \"更改阵营\". Evidence \"DEBUG -- Alter Faction\".\n\nQ013 claim_type ADDITION. target_span \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解的文字\". Correction \"你看不懂的文字：\".\n\nQ017 claim_type ADDITION. target_span \"你永远无法理解的文字\". Correction \"你无法理解的文字\".\n\nQ019 claim_type ADDITION. target_span \"即使我不会提取宝石，\". Actually span must be verbatim in target: \"即使我不会提取宝石，也可以\" — I'll use \"即使我不会提取宝石\". Is \"即使我不会提取宝石\" verbatim? Target: \"即使我不会提取宝石，也可以让...\" yes substring \"即使我不会提取宝石\" present.\n\nQ014: target \"为马基·埃亚尔的传说捐赠至少 16 欧元，达到白银捐赠等级。\" span \"达到白银捐赠等级\" present.\n\nItems with empty candidates: Q001, Q002, Q003, Q005, Q007, Q008, Q009, Q012, Q015, Q018. That's 10 empty, 10 with findings. Observations required (minLength 1) for all.\n\nLet me double check Q015: \"Earned the rank of Destroyer in the arena.\" → \"在竞技场中获得“毁灭者”称号。\" fine. Q018 fine.\n\nQ007: \"You must wear this object to use it!\" — target \"你必须装备这件物品才能使用它！\" — wear → 装备 fine.\n\nQ001: \"after letting her grow as powerful as possible\" — \"让她成长到尽可能强大之后\" would be more precise; target \"在莎西·凯希成长到尽可能强大之后杀死她\" omits \"letting\" (agency) but \"让\" implied. Fine, empty.\n\nQ005 reconsider once more: \"Learned\" → \"阅读了\" — reading ≠ learned but in game context reading lore = learning it. Also \"Spellblaze Chronicles\" → \"有关魔法大爆炸的...文献\" — \"Chronicles\" dropped, \"8章文献\" retains. Acceptable. Empty.\n\nQ009 — empty. Q012 — empty.\n\nWrite JSON."}}
