says simply \"which you do not understand\". Target adds \"even if you know Shertul you cannot understand\" — that contradicts the code showing that knowing Shertul yields the translated text. FINDING: ADDITION (or VALUE). Evidence: \"(not game.player:attr(\\\"speaks_shertul\\\") and _t[[[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]]] or _t[[#{italic}#'And AMAKTHEL made the SHER'TUL...\" — shows that when the player does understand Shertul, translated text is provided. I'll report FINDING ADDITION. Correction: \"你看不懂的文字：\" or \"你无法理解的文字：\".\n\nQ014: source \"Donated at least 16 euros to Tales of Maj'Eyal.\" target \"为马基·埃亚尔的传说捐赠至少 16 欧元，达到白银捐赠等级。\" — context: this is GOLD_DONATOR achievement (name = \"Gold Donator\", desc = SOURCE_MATCH_1). Target says \"达到白银捐赠等级\" (reached Silver donation tier) — contradicts context where Silver Donator is a separate achievement with 6 euros. FINDING: ADDITION/VALUE. target_span \"达到白银捐赠等级\", evidence: \"name = \\\"Silver Donator\\\", id = \\\"SILVER_DONATOR\\\"\" separate. Correction: remove \"，达到白银捐赠等级\" or say 黄金. Actually 16 euros = Gold tier. FINDING.\n\nQ015: \"Earned the rank of Destroyer in the arena.\" target \"在竞技场中获得“毁灭者”称号。\" — fine.\n\nQ016: \"DEBUG -- Alter Faction\" target \"调试模式 -- 锁定阵营\" — \"Alter\" → \"锁定\" (lock). ALTER ≠ lock. FINDING: ACTION. Evidence: the dialog lists factions and changes them (function _M:use... likely changes player faction). Context shows \"Alter Faction\" title. \"锁定阵营\" means lock faction. Correction: \"调试 -- 更改阵营\". FINDING.\n\nQ017: source \"which you do not understand: ...\" target \"你永远无法理解的文字：...\" — \"永远\" (never/forever) added. Source: \"which you do not understand\" — simple present. Target adds \"永远\" (can never understand). Addition. Is it disprovable? Context: if speaks_shertul, translated text given, so you could understand. But similar to Q013. Hmm, \"永远无法理解\" is a stronger claim not in source. Is this objective defect? The source says \"you do not understand\" — present state. Target says \"you will never be able to understand\" — different claim. I'd say FINDING ADDITION... or UNCERTAIN. Compare Q013 where the addition \"即使你懂夏·图尔语\" actively contradicts code. For Q017, \"永远\" is an addition without contradiction support... but code structure (translation provided when speaks_shertul) does undermine \"永远\". Both could be FINDING. But maybe be careful: the narrator might mean the strange runes are inherently incomprehensible. Actually for shertul-fortress-4, there's a translation branch, so with the talent you DO understand. So \"永远\" contradicts. I'll report FINDING ADDITION for both Q013 and Q017. For Q017 correction: \"你无法理解的文字：\".\n\nActually wait — for Q013, is the addition contradicted? The source_context shows shertul-fortress-3 with SOURCE_MATCH_1 being \"which you do not understand: ...\". The or-branch is the translation. So yes, understanding Shertul → translation. Contradiction supported. But hmm, subtle: \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解\" — could be flavor. Still, the evidence supports that knowing the language yields understanding. I'll mark FINDING for Q013 too. Alternatively UNCERTAIN for both to be safe? Rule 4: FINDING when evidence sufficient. The code structure directly shows understanding is possible via speaks_shertul. I'll go FINDING for both. Hmm, for Q013 the addition specifically contradicts; for Q017 \"永远\" also contradicts the availability of translation. Both FINDING, claim_type ADDITION.\n\nQ018: \"Got a character to level 50.\" target \"角色达到50级。\" fine.\n\nQ019: source \"Would it be possible for my Transmogrification Chest to automatically extract gems?\" target \"即使我不会提取宝石，也可以让我的转化之盒自动提取宝石吗？\" — addition \"即使我不会提取宝石\". Context: cond = \"player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS)\" — the question only appears if the player DOES know the Extract Gems talent! So the addition \"even if I don't know how to extract gems\" directly contradicts the condition. FINDING: ADDITION/CONDITION. Evidence: \"player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS)\". Correction: \"能让我的转化之盒自动提取宝石吗？\".\n\nQ020: \"The Legend of Garkul\" target \"加库尔的八章传说\" — \"八章\" (eight chapters) added; context desc says \"Learned the five chapters of the Legend of Garkul\" and lists garkul-history-1..5. FINDING: ADDITION. Correction \"加库尔的传说\".\n\nNow recheck Q005: \"Learned the eight chapters\" → \"阅读了有关魔法大爆炸的8章文献。\" Eight → 8 fine. \"Chronicles\" dropped but \"文献\" approximates. \"Learned\" → \"阅读了\" — hmm. Achievement desc pattern; other items? Not visible. I'll consider it acceptable. Leave candidates empty? Observation can note. Actually rule: no reportable objective problem → empty array. I'll leave empty.\n\nQ002: check more carefully. \"That addlepated beardling\" — beardling is a dwarf term; speaker Gorran insulting the dwarf Sodelost. \"毛脸小子\" — beardling = young beardless dwarf. \"毛脸\" (hairy face) is kind of opposite but insulting either way. Not objective. \"The finest eyes of the Iron Throne, able to read the sign of the tavern in Last Hope from the tavern in Derth!\" target: \"还说自己是钢铁王座眼力最好的家伙，坐在德斯镇的酒馆里就能看清最后的希望城酒馆的招牌！\" — \"from the tavern in Derth\" i.e., reading Last Hope's tavern sign from Derth's tavern. Target: \"坐在德斯镇的酒馆里就能看清最后的希望城酒馆的招牌\" — correct. OK empty.\n\nQ008: \"Click to copy to clipboard\" → \"点击复制\" — omits clipboard. Minor omission; \"点击复制\" implies copy. The popup later says \"Copied to clipboard!\". I'd leave empty. Also \"they can play\" → \"你们可以用\" — subject shift from \"they (friends)\" to \"你们 (you and friends)\". Target: \"这样你们可以用同一套技能组合进行游玩\" — \"你们\" includes the player; source \"they\" refers to friends. Minor. Not clearly a defect. Empty.\n\nQ009: I'll leave empty. Hmm, \"Spare me the small talk\" → \"我不是来和你们聊天的\" — Actually this changes a dismissive imperative into a declarative. The communicative function is similar (refusing small talk). I'll not report.\n\nQ006 double check: statuses map generic; \"Quest #CIMSON#Failed!\" — target \"主线任务\" — adding 主线. The dialog is for all quests (engine Quest dialog). Context 