u will never be able to understand\" — different claim. I'd say FINDING ADDITION... or UNCERTAIN. Compare Q013 where the addition \"即使你懂夏·图尔语\" actively contradicts code. For Q017, \"永远\" is an addition without contradiction support... but code structure (translation provided when speaks_shertul) does undermine \"永远\". Both could be FINDING. But maybe be careful: the narrator might mean the strange runes are inherently incomprehensible. Actually for shertul-fortress-4, there's a translation branch, so with the talent you DO understand. So \"永远\" contradicts. I'll report FINDING ADDITION for both Q013 and Q017. For Q017 correction: \"你无法理解的文字：\".\n\nActually wait — for Q013, is the addition contradicted? The source_context shows shertul-fortress-3 with SOURCE_MATCH_1 being \"which you do not understand: ...\". The or-branch is the translation. So yes, understanding Shertul → translation. Contradiction supported. But hmm, subtle: \"即使你懂夏·图尔语也无法理解\" — could be flavor. Still, the evidence supports that knowing the language yields understanding. I'll mark FINDING for Q013 too. Alternatively UNCERTAIN for both to be safe? Rule 4: FINDING when evidence sufficient. The code structure directly shows understanding is possible via speaks_shertul. I'll go FINDING for both. Hmm, for Q013 the addition specifically contradicts; for Q017 \"永远\" also contradicts the availability of translation. Both FINDING, claim_type ADDITION.\n\nQ018: \"Got a character to level 50.\" target \"角色达到50级。\" fine.\n\nQ019: source \"Would it be possible for my Transmogrification Chest to automatically extract gems?\" target \"即使我不会提取宝石，也可以让我的转化之盒自动提取宝石吗？\" — addition \"即使我不会提取宝石\". Context: cond = \"player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS)\" — the question only appears if the player DOES know the Extract Gems talent! So the addition \"even if I don't know how to extract gems\" directly contradicts the condition. FINDING: ADDITION/CONDITION. Evidence: \"player:knowTalent(player.T_EXTRACT_GEMS)\". Correc